comments.message:
Can you please rather define this to the value `1` when enabled or `0` when not. From there we can do:

```
if constexpr (NVME_SMBUS_SPEC == 1) {
    if (::ioctl(...) < 0) {
        lg2::warning(...);
     }
}
```

This makes sure it is always visible to the compiler and we won't have untested issues with syntax creeping in.

> That is to bypass the CI failure [readability-implicit-bool-conversion,-warnings-as-errors]

Right, but the warning is correct, and unless I'm missing something, it exposed a bug in the code.

> I'm not following this, I don't think I'm calculating PEC in userspace. 

You are appending a byte to the command buffer that is sent.

> decodeBasicQuery` does not have the sensor info so they have to cooperate with an agreement that there's one smbusPEC byte in the data array of 7 bytes.

This is the problem.  The "agreement" needs to be in a struct somewhere, not just a magic byte at the end of the array.

struct {
   std::array<unit8_t, ...> buf;
   boolean pecRequred;
};

Would be my initial thought.
